When you design a Formation, battlefield, desert fortress, burial pit, glass garden, caravan route, training ground, or ambush site, you may use one Sand technique as the conceptual seed.

The project may include one Sand-themed benefit, such as:

warning tracks;

collapsing dunes;

sand-hidden vault doors;

glass alarm chimes;

concealed burial traps;

heat-mirage screens;

quicksand corridors;

sand-memory witness zones.

This Insight does not create the project automatically. It requires materials, time, anchors, labor, maintenance, and at least one vulnerability chosen from exposed Anchor, water saturation, high wind, excavation, disrupted maintenance, or a weakness printed by the project rules. (Outside fights: a design seed for Formations and building projects.)

At the end of a Full Cultivation Session, prepare one **Archive Question** concerning a named creature, place, item, technique, sect, historical event, law, lineage, Formation, or cultivation phenomenon.

Before your next Full Cultivation Session, when the question becomes relevant, choose one result category:

- direct clue;
- documented precedent;
- investigation avenue;
- known weakness category;
- historical relationship;
- legal or sectarian obligation; or
- scholarly inference.

Resolve the question from records that actually exist in the setting. The adjudicator provides one truthful result in the chosen category. If no relevant record exists, the result is: **No surviving record**, followed by the nearest documented lead that can be investigated. A scholarly inference must be labeled as inference.

This Insight cannot fabricate lost knowledge, reveal a Secret erased from every record, or provide information no archive, witness record, or documented precedent could contain. (Outside fights: research questions prepared at a Full Cultivation Session and answered from records.)

When designing a Formation, ritual hall, bell tower, drum terrace, concert court, funeral rite, or morale project, use one Music principle you know as a seed concept.

Choose one principle from:

Measure;

Tone;

Chord;

Dissonance;

Echo Performer;

Battle Cadence;

Soul-Sound;

Silence-Breaking Note.

This does not create the project automatically.

The project still requires time, materials, site access, a power source whose Source CL is at least the project's Source CL, and maintenance. (Outside fights: a design seed for Formations and building projects.)

When designing a Formation, road, gate, wall, tomb, courtyard, sect foundation, battlefield camp, or long-term terrain project, use one Earth Foundation, Burden, or Settlement principle as a seed concept.

This does not create the project automatically.

The project still requires:

terrain physically connected to the project footprint;

preparation time;

material costs;

labor or Formation anchors;

maintenance;

a clear vulnerability or counterplay condition. (Outside fights: a design seed for Formations and building projects.)
